
Courses
Each course is three weeks long and consists of 12 learning hours, including 4.5 hours of live sessions with the instructor. You can expect to spend four hours on your studies each week. 
1. Theories of Adult Learning 
2. Understanding Diversity and Inclusion 
3. Program Design
4. Instructional Methods
5. Effective Facilitation
6. Evaluating Learning
7. Designing and Teaching Online
8. Indigenous Teaching and Learning Perspectives
Source: Dalhousie Open Learning and Career Development: https://www.dal.ca/study/faculties/open-learning-and-career-development/courses-certificates-diplomas/adult-education.html#adult-education
